    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0293" n="35" xml:id="pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1782</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-20T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1915, 12 noon</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>284. It is believed Chamber which meets to-day will sustain Government’s action,
                    probably appointing a committee to hear statement of its program including
                    credits to be asked, and that the committee will report favorably and its report
                    will be sustained to-morrow. Senate will then vote and war will almost certainly
                    follow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
